          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Political Neutrality</strong><br>\nAs a constitutional monarch, Elizabeth II has been strictly neutral with respect to political matters. She has been served by over a dozen UK Prime Ministers and has performed the ceremonial duty of opening and dissolving the UK parliament. Her private weekly meetings with the Prime Minister are a traditional outlet for confidential counsel and advice.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Longevity and Milestones</strong><br>\nQueen Elizabeth II is the longest-reigning monarch in British history, having surpassed Queen Victoria's record on September 9, 2015. Her reign has seen significant social, economic, and technological changes, with Elizabeth adapting to each new challenge. Milestones such as the Silver, Golden, and Diamond Jubilees have marked her time on the throne, celebrated with ceremonies and festivities.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and the Future of the Monarchy</strong><br>\nElizabeth II's legacy is marked by her commitment to duty and service, reflected in the numerous charities she supports. As she has aged, she has begun to pass more responsibilities to the younger royals. Debates about the future role and funding of the monarchy continue, but Elizabeth's personal dedication remains a cornerstone of her tenure as queen.</p>\n"
              },
